{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@","kind":"attribute"},{"text":"MainActor","kind":"attribute","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MISOButton","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"mentions","mentions":["doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/documentation\/MISOComponents\/Layouts","doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/documentation\/MISOComponents\/Actions"]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Appearances","anchor":"Appearances","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Five appearances are proposed for all layouts:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"default (by default)","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Default buttons are used for actions which are not mandatory or essential for the user.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"strong","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Should be singular and prominent, limited to one per view.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"It should be reserved for the most critical action, such as “Next,” “Save,” “Submit,” etc. It is a “call for action”.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"brand","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": A brand primary color alternative to the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"strong","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" button.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"To be used sparingly for high-value specific actions or to visually anchor a brand moment. Do not use it as the default primary button in your interfaces.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A button with ","type":"text"},{"code":"MISOButton.Appearance.Brand","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" appearance is not allowed as a direct or indirect child of an ","type":"text"},{"code":"MISOColoredSurface","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"minimal","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Minimal buttons are commonly used for actions that are considered less crucial. They can be used independently or together with a strong button.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"negative","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Negative buttons should be used sparingly to warn of a destructive action,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for example, delete or remove, typically resulting in the opening of a confirmation dialog.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A button with ","type":"text"},{"code":"MISOButton.Appearance.Negative","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" appearance is not allowed as a direct or indirect child of an ","type":"text"},{"code":"MISOColoredSurface","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"Code-samples","level":2,"text":"Code samples","type":"heading"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["    \/\/ Icon only with default appearance","    MISOButton(image: MISOImage(asset: Image(\"ic_heart\")), accessibilityLabel: \"Like\", appearance: .default) { \/* the action to process *\/ }","    \/\/ Or simpler","    MISOButton(image: MISOImage(asset: Image(\"ic_heart\")), accessibilityLabel: \"Like\") { \/* the action to process *\/ }","    \/\/ With an image to keep raw without tint","    MISOButton(image: MISOImage(asset: Image(\"il_someImage\")), accessibilityLabel: \"Like\", renderingMode: .original) { \/* the action to process *\/ }","","    \/\/ Text only with negative appearance","    MISOButton(text: \"Delete\", appearance: .negative,  style: .default) { \/* the action to process *\/ }","    \/\/ Or simpler","    MISOButton(text: \"Delete\", appearance: .negative) { \/* the action to process *\/ }","","    \/\/ A small loading button with indeterminate progress","    MISOButton(text: \"Delete\", style: .loading(), size: .small) { \/* the action to process *\/ }","","    \/\/ A small loading button with a progress (i.e. percent of progress)","    MISOButton(text: \"Delete\", style: .loading(progress: 0.75), size: .small) { \/* the action to process *\/ }","","    \/\/ Text and icon with strong appearance","    MISOButton(text: \"Validate\", image: MISOImage(asset: Image(\"ic_heart\")), appearance: .strong) { \/* the action to process *\/ }","","    \/\/ Text and icon with strong appearance and button taking full width","    MISOButton(text: \"Validate\", image: MISOImage(asset: Image(\"ic_heart\")), appearance: .strong, isFullWidth: true) { \/* the action to process *\/ }","","    \/\/ Localizable from bundle can also be used","    MISOButton(LocalizedStringKey(\"validate_button\"), bundle: Bundle.module, appearance: .strong) { }"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you need to flip your icon depending to the layout direction or not (e.g. if RTL mode lose semantics  \/ meanings):"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["    @Environment(\\.layoutDirection) var layoutDirection","","    MISOButton(text: \"Button\",","               image: MISOImage(asset: Image(systemName: \"figure.handball\"), flipped: layoutDirection == .rightToLeft))"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"text":"Sizes","anchor":"Sizes","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two sizes of button are proposed for all layouts:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Default","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": This is the default size of the component. This size is used for the vast majority of applications.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"small","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": This size can be particularly useful in an information-dense interface or in the construction of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a template or component requiring the use of small elements (in an “List item” component, for example).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"level":2,"text":"Styles","anchor":"Styles","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two style are available:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"default (by default)","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": used in the normal usage of button. The aspect of the button changes for  states ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"disabled","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"pressed","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"hovered","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" or normal (i.e. ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"enabled","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":")","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"loading","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": used after button was clicked (and probably data are requested before navigate to a next screen or get updated data, etc.).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"level":2,"text":"Rounded layout","anchor":"Rounded-layout","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Buttons can have rounded layouts to be favored in more emotional, immersive contexts or those tied to specific visual identities."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"For standard or business-oriented journeys, keep the default corners."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"This evolution addresses the need for flexibility in adapting the design to some brand contexts."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To activate the rounded button behavior, set to true the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hasRoundedButtons"},{"type":"text","text":" values of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tuning"},{"type":"text","text":" object"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in your theme configuration (if the theme exposes this property at init)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Colored surface","anchor":"Colored-surface","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If button is placed on colored surface using "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MISOColoredSurface"},{"type":"text","text":", the default colors (content, background and border) are automatically adjusted to switch to monochrome mode."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Remark: Today it is not allowed to place a Negative nor a Brand button on a colored surface."}]}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Specific behavior","anchor":"Specific-behavior","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For accessibility reasons, if the system settings for reducing motion is enabled, the loading indicator does not move.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"For ecodesign reasons, if the device is in low power mode, the loading indicator does not move.","type":"text"}]},{"style":"note","name":"Version","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"3.3.0 (Figma component design version)"}]}]},{"type":"aside","name":"Since","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDS 0.10.0"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note"}]}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:14MISOComponents10MISOButtonV","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MISOButton"}],"title":"MISOButton","roleHeading":"Structure","platforms":[{"name":"iOS","introducedAt":"15.0","deprecated":false,"beta":fa